# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch F."""
DESC_F = {
    "RT": {
        212: "A prototype developed by the Earth Alliance, combining the upper body of a mobile suit (a Strike Dagger) with the lower body of a mobile armor.\nIts Positron Reflector grants it high defensive power, and it was deployed mainly for base defense. Unlike the Positron Reflector used by the Zamza-Zah, this one deploys to the front, allowing for quick switching between offense and defense.\nIt also carries a wide array of ranged weapons, making it unmatched in long-range combat.",
        213: "A mass-produced giant mobile armor developed by the Earth Alliance.\nIt lacks the visual impact of the Zamza-Zah or Gells-Ghe, but its large beam cannon and Positron Reflector give it a good balance of offense and defense, along with excellent mobility. However, it carries no armament suited for close combat, leaving it weak at close range.",
        214: "A giant mobile suit that the Earth Alliance and LOGOS had developed by Adukarf Mechano-Industry. The listed overall length covers only the unit itself; including the back-mounted weapons unit, its size exceeds 50 meters.\nThe overwhelming firepower of its numerous full-body armaments, its thick armor, and the Positron Reflectors mounted on both arms let it maintain a high standard of both offense and defense. In its mobile armor mode, in which the back-mounted weapons unit covers the upper body, it is also capable of low-altitude flight.\nIt is a machine exclusive to Extended pilots. Stellar boarded the first unit built and engulfed cities across western Eurasia, including Berlin, in flame. The five units built afterward were committed to the battle at Heaven's Base, where Sting and others piloted them and inflicted massive damage on the ZAFT fleet.",
        215: "ZAFT's newest warship, built to operate and coordinate with the 'Second Stage Series' units. It is equipped with catapults compatible with the Silhouette System and a Deuterion beam transmission system.\nIt can move at high speed regardless of environment, whether in space, on land, or at sea. Its armament is equally abundant: the positron cannon 'Tannhauser', beam cannons, solid rounds, Gatling cannons, and a wide variety of missiles for space, ground, interception, and torpedo use, among a great deal more. In addition, the bridge - traditionally a warship's greatest weakness - is shielded during combat, making this an all-purpose warship that can fight without worry.",
        216: "A special warship operated by Phantom Pain, a special forces unit of the Earth Alliance. Talia referred to it as 'Bogey One' during pursuit.\nIt is equipped with Mirage Colloid, banned by treaty, and excels at stealth operations using it. The ship also contains a maintenance room for Extended pilots, allowing mental conditioning and memory manipulation to be carried out at any time.\nIt was used in the seizure of the new Gundams at Armory One, and fulfilled that role admirably.",
        217: "A special assault carrier built for mobile suit operations, constructed at the neutral colony Heliopolis by Orb's Morgenroete at the request of the Atlantic Federation during the previous war.\nAfter the previous war ended, it was repaired with Cagalli's support and hidden on the seabed off Orb. But with the return of a chaotic era, its former crew were gathered once more and it took to the skies again. At the time, Murrue - with the battle-hardened veteran Waltfeld aboard - proposed giving up the captain's seat, but in the end the entire bridge crew agreed that Murrue should remain in command.\nEquipped with Laminated Armor, positron cannons, and numerous other powerful systems, it still displays high combat capability even two years after its construction. Its appearance has changed little, but it has gained submersion capability and had its various electronic systems upgraded. Living conditions aboard have also been improved, the crowning example being, of all things, a hot spring. One cannot help but wonder what would happen if it attempted another barrel roll in its current state.",
        218: "A ZAFT-developed ship dedicated to operating the Freedom Gundam and Justice Gundam. Many former ZAFT crew members are aboard, including Lacus, the symbol of the Clyne Faction, Captain Waltfeld, and Dacosta and Meyrin.\nThough it is outgunned by the Archangel, it possesses enough speed to easily outrun ZAFT's fast Nazca-class ships. It also carries the Freedom Gundam and Justice Gundam's weapons unit, the 'Meteor', mounted on its bow; the unit detaches when the two Gundams make use of it, but otherwise serves as a gun battery.",
        219: "A high-speed combat vessel of ZAFT.\nA considerable number have been deployed since the previous war, with emphasis placed on mobility and mobile suit operation rather than firepower.\nThe Voltaire, flagship of the Joule Team led by Yzak, is also a Nazca-class vessel.",
        220: "A large space carrier of ZAFT, the Gondwana-class.\nEquipped with four mobile suit decks, sixteen catapults, and mobility sufficient for fleet operations, it is the ship that forms the core of ZAFT's space combat forces.",
        221: "A small space warship of the Earth Alliance.\nOriginally an escort vessel, it was refitted into a mobile-suit carrier by adding catapults and a hangar, and now serves a wide variety of purposes.\nVariants equipped with a reflector shield on the bow have also been confirmed.",
        222: "A space carrier of the Earth Alliance.\nOriginally designed as a carrier for mobile armors, it boasts one of the largest mobile suit capacities among all ships in Alliance service.",
        223: "An Overman that Duke Medaille kept hidden at Dome Polis Ulgusk, disguised as a work of art.\nWhen Gainer activated it, he combined his own name with the title 'King', earned as a game champion, to name it 'King Gainer'.\nIts weapons include the Chain Gun, usable as both a sword and a gun; the Needler, wielded like a dagger; and buckshot grenades that scatter numerous bomblets. Spare units of each are carried in a pouch on the left thigh, allowing it to fight dual-wielding two Chain Guns, among other tactics.\nIts Over Skill, 'Acceleration', lets it move at such tremendous speed that it leaves afterimages.",
        224: "A Silhouette Machine used by the Gauli Squad.\nOperated with defense rather than offense as its purpose, it is unusual among both Overmen and Silhouette Machines in carrying a shield, giving it high defensive performance.\nIt mounts a 12.7mm machine gun on its body and carries a 60mm Rivet Gun as a handheld weapon. Though it lacks a decisive finishing blow, its well-balanced overall performance makes it seem quite easy to handle.\nLater, Mamadou developed an anti-Silhouette Machine weapon that uses electromagnetic waves to interfere with the startup of Muscle Engines, giving the Panther more opportunities to shine offensively as well.",
        225: "A Silhouette Machine piloted by Gain.\nIt was developed with sniping in mind, using a 76mm rapid-fire cannon with excellent range and power. Its mobility allows it to fire while on the move, quickly relocate to terrain suited for sniping, and brace itself on both arms to serve as a fixed gun platform.\nIts eye-catching, oversized left arm belongs to the legendary Early Overman, Brunhilde, granting it monstrous strength that surpasses even other Overmen.",
        226: "A patchwork Overman assembled by combining Gachiko with parts from various other Overmen.\nIts name carries on that of an Overman Gain once used as his personal machine, and is thought to contain the meaning of 'Emperor'.\nIts main armament is a 76mm rapid-fire cannon and the Brunhilde left arm carried over from Gachiko. That arm in particular has had its abilities analyzed and properly reconnected, making the 'Gravity' Over Skill usable.",
        227: "The Siberian Railway Guard's mainstay Silhouette Machine.\nDesigned primarily to chase down People, it emphasizes mobility with features such as hover locomotion and lightweight armor.\nHowever, it has many operational shortcomings, such as poor durability and the need for two operators - one for weapons control and one for mobility. Because of this, the Dobeck was later developed as a successor.",
        228: "An upgraded Silhouette Machine based on the Dogozzo.\nThough its mobility falls short of the Dogozzo's, nearly all of the earlier machine's shortcomings have been improved, including increased armor and firepower and a switch to single-seat operation.\nA transformation mechanism also lets it switch between a normal 'Turtle Mode' with its upper section closed and a firing mode with the upper section deployed for its 200mm rocket-assisted cannon.\nAfter Adette stole a large number of units from the Siberian Railway Guard's secret base, the Dobeck Squad that was originally meant to be formed and deployed had its scale drastically reduced.\nUnits belonging to the Siberian Railway Guard are painted light blue.",
        229: "A Silhouette Machine upgraded from the Dogozzo.\nProcured as a fighting force by Adette, who became the leader of a vigilante group formed by the People of Dome Polis Gangaran.\nThe unit Adette pilots is a high-performance variant with improvements such as hover boosters, and is colored red.",
        230: "A Silhouette Machine that is an upgraded version of the Dogozzo.\nProcured by Adette, who became the leader of a vigilante group formed by the People of Dome Polis Gangaran, to serve as its fighting force.\nThe performance of the units piloted by members of Adette's squad remains unchanged from the time of procurement, but their color has been changed to dark green.",
        231: "An Overman of the Siberian Railway Guard.\nIts Over Skill, 'Time Stop', halts the passage of time for anything touched by the Stop Beam fired from its hand. Yassaba wielded this Over Skill with great skill, using it to stop bullets fired at himself, to freeze weather phenomena like storms or avalanches on snowy mountains in order to lure enemies in, and to release the stop effect at the perfect moment to create an opening. Wearing a dedicated Stop Coat allows it to fire the Stop Beam over an even wider area.\nAttacks from the four twin-barrel launchers mounted on both hands and the superheated flamethrower 'Bellows' drove King Gainer into a desperate situation.",
        232: "A mass-produced Overman of Saint Reigan, and a simplified version of the Golem. Its distinctive flight form, sitting cross-legged, resembles a great Buddha statue.\nBeing a simplified model, its appearance seems poorer than the Golem's, but its powerful Over Skill, 'Shockwave', lets a pair of units combine to unleash an ultra-vibration shockwave called the 'Mach Band Shaker'.\nSince it cannot use its Over Skill alone, it is clear that this machine only shows its true worth when operated in numbers.",
        233: "An Overman used by Saint Reigan.\nIt possesses the Over Skill 'Hardening', which can dramatically increase the strength of its full-body armor.\nA pure combat type equipped with two Hand Guns and a chakram-like Disc Harpoon. The Disc Harpoon is a versatile weapon that can change size, extend spikes to increase its power, and even be used as a close-combat weapon. It can also make use of an anti-Overman rifle.\nWearing a Power Coat unlocks the 'Superhuman Strength' Over Skill, power strong enough to lift the ceiling of Yapan. However, it was discovered to hinder mobility and close-combat capability, and was eventually cast off mid-battle.",
        234: "An Overman owned by the Siberian Railway Guard, referred to together with Desnetta Lionnetter as a 'Psycho Overman'.\nIts Over Skill, 'Mind Voice', can release a person's surface thoughts as speech, leaving their mind's contents laid bare to everyone around them. Kashmar used this to instigate conflict between the ceiling of Yapan and the People of Gangaran.\nIn combat, it also demonstrated the offensive use of reading an enemy's thoughts in advance, showing combat ability high enough to fend off attacks even from Gain and Gainer working together.",
        235: "An Overman of the Siberian Railway Guard.\nIts only real weapon is an electric shock orb fired from its whisker-like appendages, but it possesses the Over Skill 'Illusion', which conjures up whatever false images the pilot wishes one after another. This lets it appear to split into multiple copies of itself, or project phantom images to confuse the enemy.",
        236: "An Overman with the Over Skill 'Theft', capable of stealing any matter, regardless of size, across space.\nIts original owner was Duke Pirwitz, lord of Polichev, but Asuham made blackmail-like demands to seize it in what amounted to theft - a fitting origin, given the machine's own ability.\nIn battle it stole a Rivet Gun from the Panther, and even stole bullets and the artificial muscle from King Gainer's shoulder.",
        237: "An Overman given by Overdevil to Sara after she was Over Frozen by Gainer.\nHaving gained the Over Skill 'Theft', which can steal any matter across space, Sara attempted to steal the very lives of the ceiling of Yapan.",
        238: "An Early Overman of the Siberian Railway Guard.\nIt possesses the Over Skill 'Change', which lets it curl into a sphere, transform parts of its body into a sword or shield, increase its own volume, and even fire off that increased volume as projectiles - a truly anything-goes versatility.\nCombined with the astonishing ability of its pilot, Cynthia, it demonstrated performance powerful enough to single-handedly wipe out Saint Reigan's Asuham Boone special forces unit.",
        239: "A mass-produced Overman based on the Dominator.\nThough simplified, it retains transformation capability and can also use the Over Skill 'Shock'.\nIt was deployed to the Kids Munt royal guard.",
        240: "A mysterious being said to have been sealed away by the first Miia.\nIt possesses a will of its own, and holds the hidden ability to open the ice gate known as the 'Icing Gate'.\nIts body had been broken apart into separate pieces, but Kids, upon learning of its existence, secretly gathered them within the Agato Crystal.\nIts Over Skill, 'Over Freeze', is a terrifying ability that halts not only the movement of matter, but also growth, evolution, portions of emotion such as conscience, and even black holes - stopping anything, tangible or intangible, without exception.",
        241: "The form Gainer took after being Over Frozen, growing to giant size and becoming an Overman.\nWhat Gainer wears is the Overcoat of the Overman Black Mail, a machine that never appeared in the game, materialized by Overdevil.",
        242: "A black Megadeus piloted by Roger Smith.\nWhen Roger shouts, \"Big O, Showtime\" into the wristwatch on his left arm, it rises from underground to stand against the enemy at his side.\nWhen Roger boards it, the words \"CAST IN THE NAME OF GOD, YE NOT GUILTY\" are displayed on the front monitor.\nIt is normally housed beneath Roger's mansion. But once Roger issues the call, it races through disused underground transit lines aboard its dedicated transporter, the 'Prairie Dog', and is carried to its destination.\nIt conceals built-in weapons such as the eye beam 'Arc Line' and the 'Cannon Party' and 'Missile Party' fired from its chest and abdomen, but its ultimate finishing move is the one-hit-kill strike 'Sudden Impact', delivered by driving its arm's Strike Pile into the target.\nFrom time to time, Big O has taken independent action as though possessed of its own will. When, where, and by whom Big O was built - not even Roger, its own pilot, knows the answer.",
        243: "A bandage-wrapped Megadeus that appeared at the ruins of John F. Kennedy International Airport.\nIt controls the bandages covering its body and fires a beam from its eyes.\nIt bound Big O with its bandages, but was engulfed in flame after taking a direct hit from a missile fired by Big O.",
        244: "A flying red Megadeus discovered by Schwarzwald.\nIf Big O is the Big of the land, then Big Duo could be called the Big of the sky.\nIt deploys main wings from both arms, transforms its four fingers into propellers, and flies using the afterburners of its powerful engines.\nIts armament includes the eye beam Arc Line, Gatling missiles fired from its chest, and megaton missiles stored in both lower legs. It can also spin its four fingers to grind down an opponent.",
        245: "The heavily damaged Big Duo, reinforced and remodeled by Paradigm Corporation's science division.\nIt retains flight capability as before its remodeling, and now wears a face guard while flying.\nBeyond its more menacing design, several changes to its performance can be seen, such as the hollowing out of its Gatling missile ports. As new weaponry, its fingers can now transform into knife edges, and its left eye has been equipped with the Artemis Arcline.\nIts cockpit employs the same interface-substitution technology Beck once used, linking Alan into the machine through countless cables and connectors.",
        246: "The white Big, piloted by Alex.\nDiscovered in a foreign land with its body scattered in pieces, Alex requested that the Union recover it. Its parts were loaded into three separate Megadeuses, which carried them to Paradigm City.\nIt was assembled at Paradigm Corporation's underground factory using every technique the science division could bring to bear, but because its core memory was missing, it ran amok on its first outing and fell into malfunction.\nIts weapons include tentacle-like beam cannons extending from its back, cannon guns that extend from its shoulders, and the Corkscrew Punch, which attacks by spinning the rotors on its arms. By using those rotors as screws, it can also move freely underwater.",
        247: "A Megadeus used by T-Bone and Dove to break Beck out of prison, also known as 'Super Beck'.\nIt was built using Heavy Metal unit parts stolen from the Wise Company.\nIts weapons include missiles stored in both sides of its chest and a beam fired from its fingertips. The beam has enough power to cut through the chain of the Moby Dick anchor, but when it struck Big O's head crystal, it was deflected.\nIt is notable for its fast retreat speed and the ability to rotate its upper body 180 degrees, a feature it used to catch Big O off guard on one occasion.",
        248: "A three-unit combining Heavy Metal unit deployed by Beck, which combines with the shout, \"Final Together!\" Beck's sports car, the 'Beck Mobile', forms the head; Dove's construction vehicle forms the chest and arms; and T-Bone's trailer forms the lower body. Beck handled the design, while Yoshifura Yakamoto Industries handled manufacturing.\nIts weapon is a crescent-moon-shaped sword formed by combining the blade-like parts on both shoulders, engraved at its center with the single character for 'Slash'. It struck a dedicated finishing pose complete with its own theme music in front of Big O, but was riddled with holes by the merciless O Thunder attack and defeated without much of a real fight.",
        249: "The prototype form of a Megadeus, buried deep within Paradigm City's underground passages in the ruins of a pavilion-like shrine. It was discovered by Schwarzwald, who had descended underground in search of the truth.\nIt awakened in response to Dorothy's sudden appearance before it, and began operating in pursuit of her memory.\nIt toyed with Big O using agile movements and electric shocks fired from its head, but in the end was destroyed by a direct hit from Big O's Missile Party.",
        250: "A form created by combining six parts taken from three foreign Megadeuses that had been destroyed by Big O.\nThe Union revived it as a warning directed at Alex.\nAfter one-sidedly attacking the disabled Big O, it attempted to bring down Paradigm Corporation's headquarters, but was destroyed by Big Fau, piloted by Alex.",
        251: "A robot built by Sandman for use against the Zeravire.\nWith Gran Kaiser as its core, four Gran Diva units unite with it to form God Gravion.\nIt is equipped with the Ergo Form system, which circulates gravitons to form a graviton field around itself, multiplying the power of its weapons many times over. While Ergo Form is active, tremendous strain is placed on both weapons and pilot, making extended use impossible.\nHowever, since Gran Kaiser itself bears no graviton burden, it has no GravCrit either.",
        252: "A super robot developed by Sandman for use against the Zeravire.\nIt is completed when four Gran Diva units unite with the core Gran Kaiser: G-Attacker as the right leg, G-Striker as the left leg, G-Driller for both arms, and G-Shadow for the chest and head.\nThrough the effect of the Ergo Form system, it can resonate the pilot's G-Factor with the gravitons to multiply the power of its weapons many times over. However, the unite state has a time limit called GravCrit; exceeding it would destroy each Gran Diva, so the union is forcibly released just before critical, a built-in weakness.\nFor attacks, it draws on the various weapons built into each Gran Diva: the highly homing 'Graviton Missile' from G-Attacker, the laser-like whip 'Graviton Viper' from G-Striker, the 'Graviton Tornado Punch', launched by spinning G-Driller, the 'Gravity Crescent', thrown from G-Shadow's wings, and the 'Graviton Arc', which releases graviton energy from the chest, among others.",
        253: "A super robot developed by Sandman in preparation for the coming showdown with his adoptive brother, Hugue.\nIt is completed when four Sol Gran Diva units unite with the core Gran Kaiser: Geo Caliber as the right leg, Geo Stinger as the left leg, Geo Javelin for both arms, and Geo Mirage for the chest and head.\nThe Ergo Form system amplifies the pilot's willpower, allowing it to unleash gravitons in an explosive release. In theory, it holds power enough not merely to destroy a planet, but even to create one. Because piloting it demands commensurate skill from its Gran Knights, Sandman kept it hidden at a lunar base until they had grown into warriors worthy of that power.\nIts main weapons include the 'Sol Graviton Cannon' mounted on both shoulders, the 'Sol Graviton Arc' fired from the chest, the 'Sol Graviton Nova', which concentrates the two, and the 'Sol Graviton Bringer', a charging attack made by spinning the drill on its left arm. The 'Choujuuken' that God Gravion wielded is, in fact, originally a weapon of Sol Gravion.",
        254: "A super robot completed when Gran Divas unite with the star-creation unit Gran Sigma, a machine capable of creating even stars, developed by a young Sandman to save his homeland of Rambius. Unlike God Gravion's blue, its color scheme is black, matching Gran Sigma.\nDespite uniting with Gran Divas running on the Phantom System, it displayed performance on par with God Gravion. This is an achievement made possible only by Gran Sigma's own unfathomable capabilities, and above all, by Sandman's own strength and skill.\nIts main weapon is the 'Graviton Lancer', formed by joining swords drawn from its waist into one. Sandman used it to effortlessly cut down a Zeravire that stood in his path with the 'Sigma Slash', a strike whose blade traces the shape of a sigma.",
        255: "The mainstay weapon of the Earth Federation Authority (EFA), a machine that could be called a mass-produced Gravion. Five units were built, all assigned to the Gran Trooper Squad. The squad leader Faye's unit is marked with red coloring in several places.\nIn addition to a highly combat-capable humanoid form, it can also transform into a highly mobile fighter-jet form.\nEach Gran Trooper carries different armament; Faye's unit has two: the 'Gravity Lang', formed by combining and throwing the parts on both shoulders, and the 'Gravity Arrow', which fires countless beam rounds. By drawing energy from every Gran Trooper unit, it can also use the 'Lightning Detonator', a weapon with 1.5 times the destructive power of the Graviton Arc.",
        256: "The smallest class of Zeravire, the Soldier Zeravire, roughly 5 to 10 meters in overall length.\nZeravire are classified by size into 'Soldier-class', 'Warrior-class', and 'Destroyer-class'. The Soldier-class serves roles such as escorting and scouting for the Warrior-class and Destroyer-class.",
        257: "The Zeravire that first invaded Earth, appearing in Episode 1, 'The Castle Where the Giant God Dwells'. Its official name is 'Sword God of Purging, Dicreel'.\nIt was once damaged by an attack from God Gravion, but healed itself and returned, having evolved.",
        258: "A Zeravire appearing in Episode 6, 'Touga's Day Off'. Its official name is 'Perceiving God of the Demon Eye, Juettal'.\nIt was created to investigate God Gravion's capabilities, and its combat ability is lower than that of other Zeravire.",
        259: "A Zeravire built specifically to counter God Gravion, appearing in Episode 13, 'Silver Fang'. Its official name is 'War God of the Duel, Hudwell'.\nIt has resistance to every weapon it has previously encountered, and gave God Gravion a hard fight.",
        260: "A Zeravire appearing in Episode 3, 'Heated Battle! The Gurabi Hot Spring!!'. Its official name is 'Dragon God of the Flame Prison, Magguard'.\nIt lurked within a magma layer and stirred volcanic activity into greater activity.",
        261: "A Zeravire appearing in Episode 7, 'The Shattered Goddess'. Its official name is 'Servant God of the Broken Vow, Zalogros'.\nIt exploited a brief opening during the unite sequence to seize Gran Kaiser, then cornered Touga with a psychic attack and heavily damaged G-Driller.",
    },
}
